00:42:24.300 --> 00:42:27.530
The reason why GP access
has improved so much

00:42:27.530 --> 00:42:29.220
is we had a plan and
we've delivered the plan,

00:42:29.220 --> 00:42:30.930
would be the short answer.

00:42:30.930 --> 00:42:31.763
So three things.

00:42:31.763 --> 00:42:33.570
So one, we invested in
cloud-based telephony,

00:42:33.570 --> 00:42:35.580
so we've moved all of,

00:42:35.580 --> 00:42:38.340
well, practically all of our GP surgeries

00:42:38.340 --> 00:42:40.050
over onto cloud-based telephony,

00:42:40.050 --> 00:42:41.310
which means then we can,

00:42:41.310 --> 00:42:43.920
if people phone, we can
then call them back.

00:42:43.920 --> 00:42:45.180
We know how many people are waiting,

00:42:45.180 --> 00:42:46.590
we've got better data to look at,

00:42:46.590 --> 00:42:48.390
around call answering times.

00:42:48.390 --> 00:42:50.400
Number two, we've changed
the operating model.

00:42:50.400 --> 00:42:52.530
So for people that have
been struggling with access,

00:42:52.530 --> 00:42:55.080
they've been supported through
the GP improvement plan

00:42:55.080 --> 00:42:56.700
and moving over to
modern general practise,

00:42:56.700 --> 00:42:59.550
which is about how you deal
with all the calls coming in,

00:42:59.550 --> 00:43:02.430
and you triage to identify greater need

00:43:02.430 --> 00:43:05.130
on the days you can see the
people that need to be seen.

00:43:05.130 --> 00:43:07.170
And then thirdly, it's
the use of technology.

00:43:07.170 --> 00:43:10.620
So we've increased the
amount of online access,

00:43:10.620 --> 00:43:12.120
but also the use of the app.

00:43:12.120 --> 00:43:15.090
So the increase in the number
of people that are accessing

00:43:15.090 --> 00:43:17.490
and ordering their repeat
prescriptions via the app

00:43:17.490 --> 00:43:19.920
takes a lot of traffic out of calls coming

00:43:19.920 --> 00:43:21.270
to general practise.

00:43:21.270 --> 00:43:22.200
And then on your second point

00:43:22.200 --> 00:43:23.970
about has this made any difference,

00:43:23.970 --> 00:43:27.690
what we've found from
the PCN test site pilots

00:43:27.690 --> 00:43:30.210
is actually for those practises
that have got their access

00:43:30.210 --> 00:43:31.710
under control and by access under control,

00:43:31.710 --> 00:43:34.050
I mean that they're answering
their call within one

00:43:34.050 --> 00:43:36.210
or within two minutes
consistently across the day,

00:43:36.210 --> 00:43:37.950
including at 8:00 AM,

00:43:37.950 --> 00:43:40.350
and that they can offer
on the day appointments

00:43:40.350 --> 00:43:41.370
of those people that need it.

00:43:41.370 --> 00:43:44.250
When they've done that, they
then have got the head space

00:43:44.250 --> 00:43:46.110
and the capacity to start to properly deal

00:43:46.110 --> 00:43:48.120
with the proactive care and start to look

00:43:48.120 --> 00:43:51.360
after their complex patients
and start to look after,

00:43:51.360 --> 00:43:54.840
and increase their management
of long-term conditions.

00:43:54.840 --> 00:43:55.950
And where they've done that,

00:43:55.950 --> 00:43:57.270
you can start to see the impact.

00:43:57.270 --> 00:44:00.450
Our problem is, and we'll talk
about this this afternoon,

00:44:00.450 --> 00:44:03.180
but our problem is that we've
got that in small pockets

00:44:03.180 --> 00:44:05.030
and what we've got to do is scale it.

